What rigorous execution would include:
1. Definition site — rename the function declaration/assignment.
2. All call sites — update every getUserData(...) invocation across the codebase (via LSP rename or a project-wide search for \bgetUserData\b).
3. Exports/imports — if the function is exported (e.g., module.exports.getUserData or a named ES module), update both the exporting module and every importing file, since the export name changes too.
4. References in strings/docs — check comments, log messages, and documentation that mention the old name (optional, and usually judged case by case).
5. Exclusions — do not touch unrelated identifiers that merely contain the substring (e.g., getUserDataById), which is why whole-word matching matters.
